CodeBrix patch 0012 - wgpu-hal's Metal queue exposes its MTLCommandQueue (wgpu-hal/src/metal/mod.rs)

WHAT: a public accessor, Queue::raw_queue(), returning the MTLCommandQueue the Metal backend submits
on (borrowed), the mirror of Device::raw_device(). Nothing else changes; patches/0013 is its one user.
WHY: wgpu-hal 29 keeps the queue in a private field (QueueShared::raw) with no accessor, so
wgpu-native's wgpuQueueGetNativeMetalCommandQueue returns NULL ("Return null until upstream adds one
back"). Without the queue, SkiaSharp cannot build a Metal GRContext on the WebGPU device, and the
CodeBrix.WebGpu.Skia owned route on macOS (Create + CreateGrContext -> ZeroCopy) cannot work.
UPSTREAM: wgpu-hal 29.0.3 has no such accessor (its pre-objc2 Metal backend had Queue::as_raw);
re-check on every bump and drop this patch when upstream exposes the queue again.

--- a/wgpu-hal/src/metal/mod.rs
+++ b/wgpu-hal/src/metal/mod.rs
@@ -484,6 +484,14 @@
             }),
             timestamp_period,
         }
+    }
+
+    /// CodeBrix (patches/0012): the `MTLCommandQueue` this queue submits on, borrowed - never release it.
+    /// wgpu-native's `wgpuQueueGetNativeMetalCommandQueue` returns it (patches/0013), so another Metal
+    /// renderer on the same device (Skia's Metal backend) can submit on the SAME queue and be ordered with
+    /// wgpu's work by Metal itself. The mirror of `Device::raw_device`.
+    pub fn raw_queue(&self) -> &ProtocolObject<dyn MTLCommandQueue> {
+        &self.shared.raw
     }
 }
 
